r services consist of customer services and administrative support services, as well as information technology services. The company was incorporated in 1925 and is based in Erie, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian William Bolash Esq. | Interim President & CEO | Age 59 | Compensation: $849,194 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $610K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $86K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Erie Indemnity Company is a large-cap financial services business with a $14.4B market cap on $4.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 19-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $571M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield is only 1.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 45% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 56% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5611483615072244},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Erie Indemnity Stock: Analyst Estimates & Ratings","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/erie-indemnity-stock-analyst-estimates-101927060.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794565167.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Erie Strategic Ventures invests in Blitzy and HiddenLayer to advance innovation in AI infrastructure","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/erie-strategic-ventures-invests-in-blitzy-and-hiddenlayer-to-advance-innovation-in-ai-infrastructure-302935988.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794488400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(ERIE) as 